SUMMARY:Johnny Knollwood & the Church of Mad Love live at Montclair Brewery
DESCRIPTION:Johnny Knollwood & the Church of Mad Love is a funky rock and roll group based out of the NYC/NJ area that draws influence from jazz\, soul\, doo-wop\, and punk. Knollwood’s influences encompass a wide variety of styles\, including artists like Rush\, Black Sabbath\, Funkadelic\, The Beach Boys\, John Coltrane\, Herbie Hancock\, and the Ramones. The Church of Mad Love’s high-energy performances have been lauded by audiences as fun\, danceable\, and highly artistic. \n$5 cover charge per person that goes directly to the artists. \nShare this:\n				Share on Facebook (Opens in new window)\n				Facebook\n			\n				Share on Bluesky (Opens in new window)\n				Bluesky\n			\n				Share on LinkedIn (Opens in new window)\n				LinkedIn\n			\n				Share on Threads (Opens in new window)\n				Threads\n			\n				Share on Nextdoor (Opens in new window)\n				Nextdoor\n			\n				Share on WhatsApp (Opens in new window)\n				WhatsApp\n			\n				Email a link to a friend (Opens in new window)\n				Email
